{"id":"a5ff0830b59a06b70ccce085926e101ef085c1a2","axis":"silent","repo":"tmux/tmux","sha":"a5ff0830b59a06b70ccce085926e101ef085c1a2","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"image-fallback.c","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@"," "," #include \"tmux.h\""," ","+/*","+ * Draw images with text when a graphical backend is unavailable. The average","+ * brightness and colour of the area of the image covering each cell is used to","+ * pick the colour and character used.","+ */","+"," /* UTF-8 characters used for image fallback. */"," static const struct utf8_data fallback_shades[5] = {"," \t{ \" \", 1, 1, 1 },"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"image-grid.c","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,19 @@"," "," #include \"tmux.h\""," ","+/*","+ * Keep image placements in the grid and draw their visible parts.","+ *","+ * Each grid has a store of placements, each of which refers to an image and","+ * links all of its spans together. Each span describes a horizontal run of","+ * image cells on one grid line.","+ *","+ * Each client has an output backend: Kitty, SIXEL or text fallback. Graphical","+ * redraws clip each visible span and pass a rectangle one cell high to the","+ * backend. The start, flush and finish callbacks let the backend do anything","+ * it needs at points during redraw.","+ */","+"," /* Next image placement index. */"," static uint64_t next_image_placement_index;"," ","@@ -149,15 +162,15 @@ static struct image_backend image_backend_sixel = {"," };"," static struct image_backend image_backend_kitty = {"," \t\"kitty\",","-\tNULL,","+\tkitty_get_flags,"," \tkitty_select,"," \tNULL,","+\tkitty_draw_rect,","+\tkitty_redraw_start,"," \tNULL,","-\tNULL,","-\tNULL,","-\tNULL,","-\tNULL,","-\tNULL,","+\tkitty_redraw_finish,","+\tkitty_scroll,","+\tkitty_free_output_state,"," \tkitty_remove_image"," };"," ","@@ -218,13 +231,15 @@ image_draw_span(struct image_backend *backend, struct tty *tty,"," \tstruct image_rect\t rect;"," "," \trect.image = span->placement->image;","-\timage_touch(rect.image);","+\trect.index = span->placement->index;"," \trect.src_x = span->source_x + start - span->x;"," \trect.src_y = span->source_y;"," \trect.sx = end - start;"," \trect.sy = 1;"," \trect.dst_x = atx + start - px;"," \trect.dst_y = aty;","+","+\timage_touch(rect.image);"," \tbackend->draw_rect(tty, &rect);"," }"," ","@@ -748,6 +763,7 @@ image_grid_mark_scroll(struct grid *gd, u_int upper, u_int lower)"," \tu_int\t\t\t y, hsize = gd->hsize;"," \tint\t\t\t redraw = 0;"," ","+\t/* Mark lines inside the scroll region. */"," \tfor (y = upper; y <= lower; y++) {"," \t\tline = gd->linedata[y].images;"," \t\tif (line == NULL)","@@ -756,6 +772,8 @@ image_grid_mark_scroll(struct grid *gd, u_int upper, u_int lower)"," \t\tTAILQ_FOREACH(span, &line->spans, line_entry)"," \t\t\tspan->placement->scroll = -1;"," \t}","+","+\t/* Mark placements which can move with the scroll region. */"," \tfor (y = upper; y <= lower; y++) {"," \t\tline = gd->linedata[y].images;"," \t\tif (line == NULL)","@@ -778,6 +796,8 @@ image_grid_mark_scroll(struct grid *gd, u_int upper, u_int lower)"," \t\t\t}"," \t\t}"," \t}","+","+\t/* Clear the temporary marks. */"," \tfor (y = upper; y <= lower; y++) {"," \t\tline = gd->linedata[y].images;"," \t\tif (line != NULL)"],"additions":27,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"image-kitty.c","lines":["@@ -19,11 +19,31 @@"," "," #include <limits.h>"," #include <math.h>","+#include <resolv.h>"," #include <stdlib.h>"," #include <string.h>"," "," #include \"tmux.h\""," ","+/*","+ * Read Kitty graphics commands and draw images on Kitty graphics clients.","+ *","+ * Each input parser keeps one unfinished transfer and maps application image","+ * and placement IDs to internal image IDs. Once an upload is completed, it is","+ * stored as an RGBA image. Each placement then uses a child image.","+ *","+ * Output caches each image and placement separately for each client. Pixels","+ * are scaled to the client's cell pixel size on upload and reused in redraws.","+ *","+ * When a redraw is started, old rectangles overlapping the redraw area are","+ * marked for deletion, then new rectangles are queued during redraw. At the","+ * end, old rectangles are removed, new images uploaded and new placements","+ * sent. If an upload would change the drawing order of overlapping images,","+ * all the affected images are deleted and uploaded again.","+ */","+","+#define KITTY_CHUNK_SIZE 3072","+"," /* State attached to an input parser. */"," struct kitty_state {"," \tchar\t\t\t\t action;","@@ -78,13 +98,504 @@ struct kitty_image_map {"," \tTAILQ_ENTRY(kitty_image_map)\t\t entry;"," };"," ","-/* Select Kitty output. */","+/* An image uploaded to a terminal. */","+struct kitty_image_cache {","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\timage_id;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\tkitty_id;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\torder_id;","+\tuint64_t\t\t\t\tindex;","+\tint\t\t\t\t\tupload;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\txpixel;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\typixel;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\tnext_placement;","+\tTAILQ_HEAD(, kitty_placement_cache)\tplacements;","+","+\tTAILQ_ENTRY(kitty_image_cache)\t\tentry;","+};","+","+/* One grid row placed on a terminal, with positions and sizes in cells. */","+struct kitty_placement_cache {","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\tid;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\tx;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\ty;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\tw;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\th;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\tsrc_x;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\t\tsrc_y;","+\tint\t\t\t\t\tpending_delete;","+","+\tTAILQ_ENTRY(kitty_placement_cache)\tentry;","+};","+","+/* Image uploads and placements for one terminal. */","+struct kitty_output {","+\tTAILQ_HEAD(, kitty_image_cache)\timages;","+\tu_int\t\t\t\tnext_id;","+\tint\t\t\t\tchanged;","+};","+","+/* Select Kitty graphics output. */","+int","+kitty_select(struct tty *tty)","+{","+\tif (tty->term != NULL && (tty->term->flags & TERM_KITTYGRAPHICS))","+\t\treturn (1);","+\treturn (0);","+}","+","+/* Get Kitty graphics output flags. */"," int","-kitty_select(__unused struct tty *tty)","+kitty_get_flags(struct tty *tty)","+{","+\tint\tflags = IMAGE_BACKEND_GRAPHICAL;","+","+\tif (tty_term_flag(tty->term, TTYC_ISCRL))","+\t\tflags |= IMAGE_BACKEND_SCROLLS;","+\treturn (flags);","+}","+","+/* Return the Kitty output state for a terminal. */","+static struct kitty_output *","+kitty_get_output(struct tty *tty)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t*ko = tty->image_data;","+","+\tif (ko == NULL) {","+\t\tko = xcalloc(1, sizeof *ko);","+\t\tTAILQ_INIT(&ko->images);","+\t\ttty->image_data = ko;","+\t}","+\treturn (ko);","+}","+","+/* Delete a Kitty image and its placements. */","+static void","+kitty_delete(struct tty *tty, u_int id)","+{","+\tchar\ts[256];","+","+\txsnprintf(s, sizeof s, \"\\033_Ga=d,d=I,i=%u,q=2\\033\\\\\", id);","+\tif (tty->flags & TTY_STARTED)","+\t\ttty_puts(tty, s);","+\telse","+\t\ttty_raw(tty, s);","+}","+","+/* Get a cached image in drawing order. */","+static struct kitty_image_cache *","+kitty_get_image(struct tty *tty, struct image *im, uint64_t index)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t\t*ko = kitty_get_output(tty);","+\tstruct kitty_image_cache\t*entry, *before;","+","+\t/* Look for this image and placement in the output cache. */","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH(entry, &ko->images, entry) {","+\t\tif (entry->image_id == image_get_id(im) &&","+\t\t    entry->index == index)","+\t\t\treturn (entry);","+\t}","+","+\t/* Create a cache entry using this terminal's cell pixel size. */","+\tentry = xcalloc(1, sizeof *entry);","+\tentry->image_id = image_get_id(im);","+\tentry->order_id = image_get_order_id(im);","+\tentry->index = index;","+\tentry->upload = 1;","+\tentry->xpixel = tty->xpixel;","+\tif (entry->xpixel == 0)","+\t\tentry->xpixel = 8;","+\tentry->ypixel = tty->ypixel;","+\tif (entry->ypixel == 0)","+\t\tentry->ypixel = 16;","+\tTAILQ_INIT(&entry->placements);","+","+\t/* Insert the entry in image and placement drawing order. */","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH(before, &ko->images, entry) {","+\t\tif (entry->order_id < before->order_id ||","+\t\t    (entry->order_id == before->order_id &&","+\t\t    entry->index < before->index))","+\t\t\tbreak;","+\t}","+\tif (before != NULL)","+\t\tTAILQ_INSERT_BEFORE(before, entry, entry);","+\telse","+\t\tTAILQ_INSERT_TAIL(&ko->images, entry, entry);","+\treturn (entry);","+}","+","+/* Send a rectangle of the cached output pixels. */","+static void","+kitty_send_placement(struct tty *tty, struct kitty_image_cache *entry,","+    struct kitty_placement_cache *kpl)","+{","+\tchar\ts[256];","+\tu_int\tpx = kpl->src_x * entry->xpixel + 1;","+\tu_int\tpy = kpl->src_y * entry->ypixel + 1;","+\tu_int\tw = kpl->w * entry->xpixel, h = kpl->h * entry->ypixel;","+","+\tdo","+\t\tkpl->id = ++entry->next_placement;","+\twhile (kpl->id == 0);","+\txsnprintf(s, sizeof s,","+\t    \"\\033_Ga=p,i=%u,p=%u,x=%u,y=%u,w=%u,h=%u,c=%u,r=%u,C=1,q=2\\033\\\\\",","+\t    entry->kitty_id, kpl->id, px, py, w, h, kpl->w, kpl->h);","+","+\ttty_cursor(tty, kpl->x, kpl->y);","+\ttty_puts(tty, s);","+}","+","+/* Record a placement to send after the redraw. */","+static void","+kitty_place(struct kitty_image_cache *entry, u_int src_x, u_int src_y,","+    u_int w, u_int h, u_int dst_x, u_int dst_y)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_placement_cache\t*kpl;","+","+\tkpl = xcalloc(1, sizeof *kpl);","+\tkpl->x = dst_x;","+\tkpl->y = dst_y;","+\tkpl->w = w;","+\tkpl->h = h;","+\tkpl->src_x = src_x;","+\tkpl->src_y = src_y;","+\tTAILQ_INSERT_HEAD(&entry->placements, kpl, entry);","+}","+","+/* Place the part of an image outside the redraw area. */","+static void","+kitty_redraw_keep_piece(struct kitty_image_cache *entry,","+    struct kitty_placement_cache *kpl, u_int x, u_int y, u_int w, u_int h)","+{","+\tif (w == 0 || h == 0)","+\t\treturn;","+\tkitty_place(entry, kpl->src_x + (x - kpl->x), kpl->src_y + (y - kpl->y),","+\t    w, h, x, y);","+}","+","+/* Preserve placement pieces outside the redraw area. */","+static void","+kitty_redraw_keep(struct kitty_image_cache *entry,","+    struct kitty_placement_cache *kpl, u_int x, u_int y, u_int w, u_int h)","+{","+\tu_int\tpx0 = kpl->x, px1 = kpl->x + kpl->w;","+\tu_int\tpy0 = kpl->y, py1 = kpl->y + kpl->h;","+\tu_int\tix0, ix1, iy0, iy1;","+","+\tix0 = (x > px0 ? x : px0);","+\tix1 = (x + w < px1 ? x + w : px1);","+\tiy0 = (y > py0 ? y : py0);","+\tiy1 = (y + h < py1 ? y + h : py1);","+\tif (ix0 == px0 && ix1 == px1 && iy0 == py0 && iy1 == py1)","+\t\treturn;","+","+\tkitty_redraw_keep_piece(entry, kpl, px0, py0, px1 - px0, iy0 - py0);","+\tkitty_redraw_keep_piece(entry, kpl, px0, iy1, px1 - px0, py1 - iy1);","+\tkitty_redraw_keep_piece(entry, kpl, px0, iy0, ix0 - px0, iy1 - iy0);","+\tkitty_redraw_keep_piece(entry, kpl, ix1, iy0, px1 - ix1, iy1 - iy0);","+}","+","+/* Mark placements for deletion after the redraw. */","+void","+kitty_redraw_start(struct tty *tty, u_int x, u_int y, u_int w, u_int h)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t\t*ko = tty->image_data;","+\tstruct kitty_image_cache\t*entry;","+\tstruct kitty_placement_cache\t*kpl;","+","+\tif (ko == NULL)","+\t\treturn;","+","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH(entry, &ko->images, entry) {","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH(kpl, &entry->placements, entry) {","+\t\t\tif (kpl->pending_delete)","+\t\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\t\tif (kpl->x >= x + w ||","+\t\t\t    kpl->x + kpl->w <= x ||","+\t\t\t    kpl->y >= y + h ||","+\t\t\t    kpl->y + kpl->h <= y) {","+\t\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\tkpl->pending_delete = 1;","+\t\t\tko->changed = 1;","+","+\t\t\t/* Preserve pieces outside the redraw area. */","+\t\t\tkitty_redraw_keep(entry, kpl, x, y, w, h);","+\t\t}","+\t}","+}","+","+/* Delete one terminal placement, retaining its uploaded pixels. */","+static void","+kitty_delete_placement(struct tty *tty, struct kitty_image_cache *entry,","+    struct kitty_placement_cache *kpl)","+{","+\tchar\ts[256];","+","+\txsnprintf(s, sizeof s, \"\\033_Ga=d,d=i,i=%u,p=%u,q=2\\033\\\\\",","+\t    entry->kitty_id, kpl->id);","+\tif (entry->kitty_id != 0 && kpl->id != 0)","+\t\ttty_puts(tty, s);","+\tTAILQ_REMOVE(&entry->placements, kpl, entry);","+\tfree(kpl);","+}","+","+/* Move cached grid rows with a terminal scroll region. */","+void","+kitty_scroll(struct tty *tty, u_int x, u_int y, u_int w, u_int h, int n)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t\t*ko = tty->image_data;","+\tstruct kitty_image_cache\t*entry;","+\tstruct kitty_placement_cache\t*kpl, *next;","+\tint\t\t\t\t py;","+","+\tif (ko == NULL || !tty_term_flag(tty->term, TTYC_ISCRL))","+\t\treturn;","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH(entry, &ko->images, entry) {","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(kpl, &entry->placements, entry, next) {","+\t\t\tif (kpl->x < x ||","+\t\t\t    kpl->x + kpl->w > x + w ||","+\t\t\t    kpl->y < y ||","+\t\t\t    kpl->y >= y + h)","+\t\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\t\tpy = (int)kpl->y - n;","+\t\t\tif (py < (int)y || py >= (int)(y + h)) {","+\t\t\t\tkitty_delete_placement(tty, entry, kpl);","+\t\t\t\tko->changed = 1;","+\t\t\t} else","+\t\t\t\tkpl->y = py;","+\t\t}","+\t}","+}","+","+/* Free a cached Kitty image. */","+static void","+kitty_free_entry(struct tty *tty, struct kitty_image_cache *entry, int send)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_placement_cache\t*kpl, *next;","+","+\tif (send && entry->kitty_id != 0)","+\t\tkitty_delete(tty, entry->kitty_id);","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(kpl, &entry->placements, entry, next) {","+\t\tTAILQ_REMOVE(&entry->placements, kpl, entry);","+\t\tfree(kpl);","+\t}","+\tfree(entry);","+}","+","+/* Free Kitty output state for a terminal. */","+void","+kitty_free_output_state(struct tty *tty, int send)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t\t*ko = tty->image_data;","+\tstruct kitty_image_cache\t*entry, *next;","+","+\tif (ko != NULL) {","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(entry, &ko->images, entry, next) {","+\t\t\tTAILQ_REMOVE(&ko->images, entry, entry);","+\t\t\tkitty_free_entry(tty, entry, send);","+\t\t}","+\t\tfree(ko);","+\t\ttty->image_data = NULL;","+\t}","+}","+","+/* Remove cached Kitty images no longer held by the server. */","+static void","+kitty_free_stale_images(struct tty *tty)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t\t*ko = tty->image_data;","+\tstruct kitty_image_cache\t*entry, *next;","+","+\tif (ko != NULL) {","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(entry, &ko->images, entry, next) {","+\t\t\tif (image_find(entry->image_id) == NULL) {","+\t\t\t\tTAILQ_REMOVE(&ko->images, entry, entry);","+\t\t\t\tkitty_free_entry(tty, entry, 1);","+\t\t\t\tko->changed = 1;","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+\t}","+}","+","+/* Check whether any placements of two images overlap. */","+static int","+kitty_images_overlap(struct kitty_image_cache *a, struct kitty_image_cache *b)"," {","+\tstruct kitty_placement_cache\t*akpl, *bkpl;","+","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH(akpl, &a->placements, entry) {","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH(bkpl, &b->placements, entry) {","+\t\t\tif (akpl->x < bkpl->x + bkpl->w &&","+\t\t\t    bkpl->x < akpl->x + akpl->w &&","+\t\t\t    akpl->y < bkpl->y + bkpl->h &&","+\t\t\t    bkpl->y < akpl->y + akpl->h)","+\t\t\t\treturn (1);","+\t\t}","+\t}"," \treturn (0);"," }"," ","+/* Upload a canvas prepared for this terminal's cell pixel size. */","+static int","+kitty_upload(struct tty *tty, struct kitty_image_cache *entry)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t*ko = tty->image_data;","+\tstruct image\t\t*im = image_find(entry->image_id);","+\tstruct image_geom\t*ig = image_get_geometry(im);","+\tchar\t\t\t s[128], e[4097];","+\tu_char\t\t\t*p, *row, *p0;","+\tsize_t\t\t\t offset, size, total, limit, stride;","+\tu_int\t\t\t x, y, w, h;","+\tu_int\t\t\t cw = entry->xpixel, ch = entry->ypixel;","+\tuint64_t\t\t width = (uint64_t)ig->sx * cw;","+\tuint64_t\t\t height = (uint64_t)ig->sy * ch;","+\tint\t\t\t elen;","+","+\t/* Check the output size and allow for a one-pixel border. */","+\tlimit = options_get_number(global_options, \"image-size-limit\");","+\tif (width > UINT_MAX - 2 ||","+\t    height > UINT_MAX - 2 ||","+\t    width * height > limit / 4)","+\t\treturn (0);","+\tw = width + 2;","+\th = height + 2;","+\tif ((uint64_t)w * h > SIZE_MAX / 4)","+\t\treturn (0);","+\tstride = (size_t)w * 4;","+\ttotal = stride * h;","+","+\t/* Allocate and scale the output pixels. */","+\tp = xmalloc(total);","+\tfor (y = 0; y < height; y++) {","+\t\trow = p + (y + 1) * stride;","+\t\tfor (x = 0; x < width; x++) {","+\t\t\tp0 = image_get_pixel(im, x, y, width, height);","+\t\t\tmemcpy(row + (x + 1) * 4, p0, 4);","+\t\t}","+","+\t\t/* Fill the side borders with copies of the edge pixels. */","+\t\tmemcpy(row, row + 4, 4);","+\t\tmemcpy(row + stride - 4, row + stride - 8, 4);","+\t}","+\tmemcpy(p, p + stride, stride);","+\tmemcpy(p + (h - 1) * stride, p + (h - 2) * stride, stride);","+","+\tentry->upload = 0;","+\tdo","+\t\tentry->kitty_id = ++ko->next_id;","+\twhile (entry->kitty_id == 0);","+","+\t/* Encode and send the pixels in base64 chunks. */","+\tfor (offset = 0; offset < total; offset += size) {","+\t\tsize = total - offset;","+\t\tif (size > KITTY_CHUNK_SIZE)","+\t\t\tsize = KITTY_CHUNK_SIZE;","+\t\telen = b64_ntop(p + offset, size, e, sizeof e);","+\t\tif (elen < 0)","+\t\t\tfatalx(\"base64 encode failed\");","+\t\tif (offset == 0) {","+\t\t\txsnprintf(s, sizeof s,","+\t\t\t    \"\\033_Ga=t,f=32,s=%u,v=%u,i=%u,q=2,m=%d;\",","+\t\t\t    w, h, entry->kitty_id, offset + size < total);","+\t\t} else {","+\t\t\tif (offset + size < total)","+\t\t\t\txsnprintf(s, sizeof s, \"\\033_Gm=1;\");","+\t\t\telse","+\t\t\t\txsnprintf(s, sizeof s, \"\\033_Gm=0;\");","+\t\t}","+\t\ttty_puts(tty, s);","+\t\ttty_putn(tty, e, elen, 0);","+\t\ttty_puts(tty, \"\\033\\\\\");","+\t}","+\tfree(p);","+\treturn (1);","+}","+","+/* Finish drawing, replacing overlapping images if needed. */","+void","+kitty_redraw_finish(struct tty *tty)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_output\t\t*ko = tty->image_data;","+\tstruct kitty_image_cache\t*entry, *other, *next_entry;","+\tstruct kitty_placement_cache\t*kpl, *next;","+\tint\t\t\t\t changed;","+","+\tif (ko == NULL)","+\t\treturn;","+\tkitty_free_stale_images(tty);","+","+\tif (!ko->changed)","+\t\treturn;","+\tko->changed = 0;","+","+\t/* Delete placements marked during the redraw. */","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(entry, &ko->images, entry, next_entry) {","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(kpl, &entry->placements, entry, next) {","+\t\t\tif (kpl->pending_delete)","+\t\t\t\tkitty_delete_placement(tty, entry, kpl);","+\t\t}","+\t\tif (TAILQ_EMPTY(&entry->placements)) {","+\t\t\tTAILQ_REMOVE(&ko->images, entry, entry);","+\t\t\tkitty_free_entry(tty, entry, 1);","+\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\t}","+\t\tif (entry->kitty_id == 0)","+\t\t\tentry->upload = 1;","+\t}","+","+\t/* Include the overlap group if an upload needs to be replaced. */","+\tdo {","+\t\tchanged = 0;","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH(entry, &ko->images, entry) {","+\t\t\tother = entry;","+\t\t\twhile ((other = TAILQ_NEXT(other, entry)) != NULL) {","+\t\t\t\tif (entry->upload && other->upload)","+\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\t\t\tif (!entry->upload &&","+\t\t\t\t    !other->upload &&","+\t\t\t\t    entry->kitty_id < other->kitty_id)","+\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\t\t\tif (!kitty_images_overlap(entry, other))","+\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\t\t\tentry->upload = other->upload = 1;","+\t\t\t\tchanged = 1;","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+\t} while (changed);","+","+\t/* Delete affected uploads and reset their placement IDs. */","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH(entry, &ko->images, entry) {","+\t\tif (!entry->upload || entry->kitty_id == 0)","+\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\tkitty_delete(tty, entry->kitty_id);","+\t\tentry->kitty_id = 0;","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH(kpl, &entry->placements, entry)","+\t\t\tkpl->id = 0;","+\t}","+","+\t/* Upload images in drawing order and send new placements. */","+\tTAILQ_FOREACH(entry, &ko->images, entry) {","+\t\tif (entry->upload && !kitty_upload(tty, entry))","+\t\t\tcontinue;","+\t\tTAILQ_FOREACH(kpl, &entry->placements, entry) {","+\t\t\tif (kpl->id == 0)","+\t\t\t\tkitty_send_placement(tty, entry, kpl);","+\t\t}","+\t}","+}","+","+/* Draw an image rectangle using the Kitty graphics protocol. */","+void","+kitty_draw_rect(struct tty *tty, struct image_rect *rect)","+{","+\tstruct kitty_image_cache\t*entry;","+","+\tentry = kitty_get_image(tty, rect->image, rect->index);","+\tkitty_get_output(tty)->changed = 1;","+\tkitty_place(entry, rect->src_x, rect->src_y,","+\t    rect->sx, rect->sy, rect->dst_x, rect->dst_y);","+}","+"," /* Parse Kitty graphics control data. */"," static int"," kitty_parse_control_data(struct kitty_state *ks, const u_char *data,","@@ -637,6 +1148,7 @@ kitty_parse_input(struct input_ctx *ictx, struct window_pane *wp,"," \t\t}"," \t}"," ","+\t/* Reset the control fields when starting a new transfer. */"," \tif (!ks->more) {"," \t\tks->action = 't';"," \t\tks->format = 32;","@@ -698,11 +1210,14 @@ kitty_parse_input(struct input_ctx *ictx, struct window_pane *wp,"," \t\tm = \"OK\";"," \t\tgoto out;"," \t}","+","+\t/* Collect the image data until the last chunk arrives. */"," \tif (psize != 0 && kitty_append_data(ks, found + 1, psize) != 0)"," \t\tgoto out;"," \tif (ks->more)"," \t\treturn;"," ","+\t/* Place an image which was uploaded earlier. */"," \tif (ks->action == 'p') {"," \t\tmap = kitty_image_map_find(ks, ks->image_id);"," \t\tif (map == NULL) {","@@ -718,6 +1233,7 @@ kitty_parse_input(struct input_ctx *ictx, struct window_pane *wp,"," \t\tgoto place;"," \t}"," ","+\t/* Decode the completed transfer into RGBA pixels. */"," \tif (ks->compression != 'o' && ks->compression != 'z')"," \t\tgoto out;"," \tlimit = options_get_number(global_options, \"image-size-limit\");"],"additions":518,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"image-sixel.c","lines":["@@ -27,6 +27,21 @@"," "," #include \"tmux.h\""," ","+/*","+ * Decode SIXEL input and draw common images as SIXEL output.","+ *","+ * The parser builds rows of palette indexes, applying raster attributes,","+ * colour definitions and repeat commands as they arrive. sixel_write","+ * converts the result to RGBA pixels, records its size using the input cell","+ * pixel size, and passes it to image_write to attach it to the grid.","+ *","+ * Output combines adjacent image rows before converting them at the client's","+ * cell pixel size. The conversion maps output pixels back to the source","+ * image, builds a palette from the visible colours, then dithers colour and","+ * alpha into palette indexes. The encoder turns those indexes into SIXEL","+ * colour planes and repeat runs.","+ */","+"," /* Maximum SIXEL width and height. */"," #define SIXEL_WIDTH_LIMIT 10000"," #define SIXEL_HEIGHT_LIMIT 10000","@@ -1412,6 +1427,7 @@ sixel_from_image(struct image *im, u_int x, u_int y, u_int sx, u_int sy,"," \tstruct sixel_image\t*si, *cached;"," \tchar\t\t\t*data;"," ","+\t/* Get a cached image, or convert just the requested cells. */"," \tcached = sixel_get_image(im, cw, ch);"," \tif (cached != NULL)"," \t\tsi = sixel_crop(cached, x, y, sx, sy, cw, ch);"],"additions":16,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"image.c","lines":["@@ -26,6 +26,20 @@"," "," #include \"tmux.h\""," ","+/*","+ * Store decoded images and map their pixels for drawing.","+ *","+ * An image contains RGBA pixels and geometry describing which part of the","+ * source image to use, its size in cells, and any scaling or padding. Child","+ * images can share a parent's pixels with different geometry. Each image has a","+ * unique ID.","+ *","+ * Scaling and offsets are recorded in the geometry. The drawing backends use","+ * the helpers here to map output cells or pixels back to the source image.","+ * This lets clients with different cell pixel sizes draw the same image","+ * without changing its stored pixels.","+ */","+"," /* An image. */"," TAILQ_HEAD(image_list, image);"," struct image {","@@ -269,6 +283,7 @@ image_create_with_parent(enum image_type type, struct image *parent,"," \tif (ig->scaled_width <= 0 || ig->scaled_height <= 0)"," \t\treturn (NULL);"," ","+\t/* Check limits before allocating the image. */"," \tif (parent == NULL)"," \t\tsize = (ig->src_h - 1) * stride + ig->src_w * 4;"," \tif (image_check_limits(parent, size) != 0)","@@ -370,6 +385,7 @@ image_get_bounds(struct image_geom *ig, u_int x, u_int y, u_int w, u_int h,"," \tif (h > sy - y)"," \t\th = sy - y;"," ","+\t/* Map the requested area and clip it to the source image. */"," \tib->left = image_map_x(ig, x, sx);"," \tib->top = image_map_y(ig, y, sy);"," \tib->right = image_map_x(ig, x + w, sx);"],"additions":16,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"regress/image-kitty-nested.sh","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@","+#!/bin/sh","+","+# Native Kitty output remains within tmux's supported input subset when nested.","+","+PATH=/bin:/usr/bin","+TERM=screen","+export PATH TERM","+[ -z \"$TEST_TMUX\" ] && TEST_TMUX=$(readlink -f ../tmux)","+command -v python3 >/dev/null || exit 101","+","+python3 -B - \"$TEST_TMUX\" <<'PY'","+import shlex","+import sys","+import time","+from image_test import image_test, kitty","+from image_kitty import KittyTerminal","+","+red, green, white = (255, 0, 0), (0, 255, 0), (255, 255, 255)","+","+","+def upload(id, colour):","+    \"\"\"Store a pixel under an application image ID.\"\"\"","+    return kitty('a=t,i=%d,f=32,s=1,v=1' % id, bytes((*colour, 255)))","+","+","+def put(id):","+    \"\"\"Place two columns using a named placement.\"\"\"","+    return kitty('a=p,i=%d,p=1,C=1,c=2,r=1' % id)","+","+","+def rectangle(colour, x=0, w=16):","+    \"\"\"Expected pixels after both tmux servers have rendered.\"\"\"","+    return {(px + x, y): colour for y in range(16) for px in range(w)}","+","+","+with image_test(sys.argv[1]) as outer, image_test(sys.argv[1]) as inner:","+    client = outer.attach(kitty_graphics=True)","+    terminal = KittyTerminal()","+    inner.run('set-option', '-as', 'terminal-features', ',*:kittygraphics')","+    command = 'env TMUX= TERM=tmux-256color ' + shlex.join(","+        inner.server + ['attach-session', '-t', 'image'])","+    outer.run('respawn-pane', '-k', command)","+    inner.wait(lambda: inner.run('list-clients', '-F', '#{client_name}') != '')","+    client.read(0.3)","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+","+    def expect(data, expected):","+        \"\"\"Wait for input and both stages of graphical output to finish.\"\"\"","+        client.clear()","+        inner.emit(data)","+        end = time.monotonic() + 10","+        while True:","+            client.read(0.05)","+            terminal.feed(client.data)","+            client.data.clear()","+            if terminal.render() == expected or time.monotonic() > end:","+                break","+        terminal.check(expected)","+","+    # An older source first becomes visible after its overlapping neighbour.","+    expect(upload(200, red) + upload(100, white) + put(100), rectangle(white))","+    expect(put(200), rectangle(white))","+    # Replacement preserves drawing order through both servers.","+    expect(upload(200, green) + put(200), rectangle(white))","+    expect(b'\\033[1;2H' + put(100), rectangle(green, w=8) |","+        rectangle(white, x=8))","+    expect(kitty('a=d,d=I,i=100'), rectangle(green))","+    expect(kitty('a=d,d=A'), {})","+PY"],"additions":69,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"regress/image-kitty-output.sh","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@","+#!/bin/sh","+","+# Native Kitty uploads, geometry, placement ordering, redraw and cleanup.","+","+PATH=/bin:/usr/bin","+TERM=screen","+export PATH TERM","+[ -z \"$TEST_TMUX\" ] && TEST_TMUX=$(readlink -f ../tmux)","+command -v python3 >/dev/null || exit 101","+","+python3 -B - \"$TEST_TMUX\" <<'PY'","+import sys","+from image_test import image_test, kitty, sixel","+from image_kitty import KittyTerminal","+","+red, green, blue, white = (255, 0, 0), (0, 255, 0), (0, 0, 255), (255, 255, 255)","+","+","+def upload(id, colour):","+    \"\"\"Store a single pixel without placing it.\"\"\"","+    return kitty('a=t,i=%d,f=32,s=1,v=1' % id, bytes((*colour, 255)))","+","+","+def put(id, controls=''):","+    \"\"\"Place two columns and one row without moving the cursor.\"\"\"","+    return kitty('a=p,i=%d,C=1,c=2,r=1' % id + controls)","+","+","+def rectangle(colour, x=0, y=0, w=16, h=16):","+    \"\"\"Expected solid pixels at a terminal pixel position.\"\"\"","+    return {(x + xx, y + yy): colour for yy in range(h) for xx in range(w)}","+","+","+with image_test(sys.argv[1]) as test:","+    client = test.attach(kitty_graphics=True)","+    terminal = KittyTerminal()","+    test.emit(upload(200, red) + upload(100, white) + put(100))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(white))","+    assert terminal.uploads == 1","+    test.emit(put(200))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(white))","+    assert terminal.uploads == 3, 'overlapping upper image was not replaced'","+    test.redraw()","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(white))","+    assert terminal.uploads == 3, 'full redraw uploaded pixels again'","+    # The older image keeps its order when replaced, but not when deleted.","+    test.emit(upload(200, green) + put(200))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(white))","+    test.emit(kitty('a=d,d=I,i=200') + upload(200, red) + put(200))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(red))","+    # Native placements survive text writes, then disappear on deletion.","+    test.emit(b'\\033[Htext underneath')","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(red))","+    test.emit(kitty('a=d,d=A'))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check({})","+    assert not terminal.images and not terminal.placements","+    # SIXEL-origin images use the same backend and ordering.","+    test.emit(b'\\033[H' + sixel(16, 16, [(0, 0, 100)], [0] * 256))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(blue))","+    test.emit(b'\\033[H' + upload(300, red) + put(300))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(red))","+    # A different window must not retain native placements from the first.","+    client.clear()","+    test.run('new-window', 'stty raw -echo; exec cat')","+    client.read(0.3)","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check({})","+    assert not terminal.images, 'hidden uploads were retained in the terminal'","+    client.clear()","+    test.run('select-window', '-t', ':0')","+    client.read(0.3)","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(rectangle(red))","+    # Transparency is preserved across separately uploaded images.","+    test.emit(kitty('a=T,i=400,f=32,s=1,v=1,c=2,r=1,C=1',","+        bytes((0, 0, 255, 128))))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    blended = rectangle((127, 0, 128))","+    terminal.check(blended)","+    # Detach deletes tmux's uploads before leaving the alternate screen.","+    client.clear()","+    test.run('detach-client', '-t', client.name)","+    try:","+        client.read(0.5)","+    except RuntimeError as error:","+        assert str(error) == 'attached client exited', error","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check({})","+    assert not terminal.images","+","+# Source position, source size, subcell offsets, transparent padding and clips.","+with image_test(sys.argv[1]) as test:","+    other = test.attach(kitty_graphics=True, cw=10, ch=20)","+    client = test.attach(kitty_graphics=True)","+    terminal = KittyTerminal()","+    term2 = KittyTerminal(cw=10, ch=20)","+    data = bytes(v for y in range(8) for x in range(12)","+        for v in ((red if x < 6 else green) if y < 4 else blue) + (255,))","+    test.emit(kitty('a=T,i=1,f=32,s=12,v=8,x=6,y=0,w=6,h=4,'","+        'c=2,r=2,X=3,Y=5,C=1', data))","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    expected = rectangle(green, x=3, y=5, w=13, h=27)","+    terminal.check(expected)","+    term2.feed(other.data)","+    expected2 = rectangle(green, x=4, y=7, w=16, h=33)","+    term2.check(expected2)","+    # Inserting text cells must not move Kitty placements.","+    test.emit(b'\\033[1;2H\\033[@')","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    terminal.check(expected)","+    term2.feed(other.data)","+    term2.check(expected2)","+    uploads = terminal.uploads, term2.uploads","+    test.redraw()","+    terminal.feed(client.data)","+    term2.feed(other.data)","+    terminal.check(expected)","+    term2.check(expected2)","+    assert uploads == (terminal.uploads, term2.uploads)","+    # A changed cell pixel size discards the old upload and prepares it again.","+    test.resize(other, 40, 16, cw=12, ch=24)","+    term2.cw, term2.ch = 12, 24","+    term2.feed(other.data)","+    term2.check(rectangle(green, x=5, y=8, w=19, h=40))","+    assert term2.uploads > uploads[1]","+PY"],"additions":135,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"regress/image-kitty-overlap.sh","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@","+#!/bin/sh","+","+# Replace overlapping Kitty uploads together, leaving other uploads cached.","+","+PATH=/bin:/usr/bin","+TERM=screen","+export PATH TERM","+[ -z \"$TEST_TMUX\" ] && TEST_TMUX=$(readlink -f ../tmux)","+command -v python3 >/dev/null || exit 101","+","+python3 -B - \"$TEST_TMUX\" <<'PY'","+import sys","+from image_test import image_test, kitty","+from image_kitty import KittyTerminal","+","+red, green, blue = (255, 0, 0), (0, 255, 0), (0, 0, 255)","+white, yellow, grey = (255, 255, 255), (255, 255, 0), (128, 128, 128)","+","+","+def upload(id, colour):","+    \"\"\"Upload new pixels under an application image ID.\"\"\"","+    return kitty('a=t,i=%d,f=32,s=1,v=1' % id, bytes((*colour, 255)))","+","+","+def put(id, x=0, y=0, c=3, r=2):"],"additions":25,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":812,"deletions":9,"truncated":true,"file_count":8},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-10-30T15:57:17.264516+00:00"}